// Title: Suspicious Usage Of Active Directory Diagnostic Tool (ntdsutil.exe)
// Sigma ID: a58353df-af43-4753-bad0-cd83ef35eef5
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-14 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003.003
// Description: Detects execution of ntdsutil.exe to perform different actions such as restoring
//   snapshots...etc.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage to restore snapshots
//   - Legitimate admin activity
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/windows/it-pro/windows-server-2012-r2-and-2012/cc731620(v=ws.11)
//   - https://symantec-enterprise-blogs.security.com/blogs/threat-intelligence/espionage-asia-governments
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_ntdsutil_susp_usage.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\ntdsutil.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "ntdsutil.exe") and ((ProcessCommandLine contains "snapshot" and ProcessCommandLine contains "mount ") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "ac" and ProcessCommandLine contains " i" and ProcessCommandLine contains " ntds"))
